properties from the database.\n\nRenters can explore properties, discover the agents behind each listing, and request inspections.\n\nBuilt with React, Tailwind CSS, Node.js, Express, MongoDB and Meta Muse Spark.\n\nThis is my project for the Meta Global AI Developer Hackathon.\n\nBuilding, learning and pushing myself to create useful technology. \ud83d\ude80\n\n#MetaAI #BuildWithMeta #FindSafeHomes #WebDevelopment"}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 102, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "I\u2019ve been building something exciting! \ud83d\ude80\n\nIntroducing FindSafeHomes an AI-powered housing marketplace built for a simpler house-hunting experience.\n\nInstead of manually filtering through countless listings, renters can describe the kind of property they need in natural language. https://t.co/4Vd3q5FVVI", "url": "https://x.com/rik22ky/status/2117595390480416976"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2117593493568655360"]}, "author_id": "1826343036508422144", "created_at": "2026-11-03T12:23:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117593499281326430"], "id": "2117593499281326430", "note_tweet": {"entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 73, "start": 68, "tag": "SHOP"}]}, "text": "The core reasons driving the sharp post earnings drop ( -18% \ud83d\udd34) for $SHOP :\n\n\ud83d\udd38Top Line Revenue Miss: \n\nShopify reported revenue of $3.74B. While this marks impressive growth, it marginally missed Wall Street's elevated consensus whisper numbers which pinned expectations closer to $3.77B\n\n\ud83d\udd38Unfavorable Revenue Mix Shifting Margins: \n\nThe explosive 53% YoY expansion of transaction heavy tools like Shop Pay and Shopify Payments has created an unfavorable revenue mix. Because payment transactions carry structurally lower gross margins than subscription software fees (due to third party bank processing costs), Shopify's overall gross profit growth came in lower than its 32% top line revenue growth.\n\n\ud83d\udd38No Margin for Error at Current Valuation: \n\nLeading into today's print, Shopify's aggressive AI integration rally (including the Meta Muse partnership) had pushed the stock to trade at an expensive valuation multiple of 86 to 115 times forward earnings/free cash flow. When a stock trades at such a steep premium, even a microscopic top line miss or margin pressure forces institutional funds to immediately protect gains and sell."}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 274, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "The core reasons driving the sharp post earnings drop ( -18% \ud83d\udd34) for $SHOP :\n\n\ud83d\udd38Top Line Revenue Miss: \n\nShopify reported revenue of $3.74B. While this marks impressive growth, it marginally missed Wall Street's elevated consensus whisper numbers which pinned expectations closer https://t.co/2iZ49q18k3", "url": "https://x.com/SagoLabsVC/status/2117593499281326430"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2117590983101575169"]}, "author_id": "2116061505154084864", "created_at": "2026-11-03T12:21:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117593082027987053"], "id": "2117593082027987053", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Muse AI One-Shot a Live Stock Screener With Real Data, Live News Feed, and All Real Stock Prices\n#MetaMuse, #MuseAI, #Muse, #MetaMuseAI, #MetaAI\n@alexandr_wang  @Muse, @finkd https://t.co/S6DWxYWeNo", "url": "https://x.com/MussyMoney/status/2117593082027987053"}, {"author_id": "151069987", "created_at": "2026-11-03T12:16:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117591702940836308"], "id": "2117591702940836308", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 40, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Meta Muse\u3092\u59cb\u3081\u3066\u307f\u307e\u3057\u305f\u3002\n\u62db\u5f85\u30b3\u30fc\u30c9 8VBBEC\n\u3053\u308c\u3092\u4f7f\u3046\u3068\u79c1\u3082\u305d\u3061\u3089\u308210\u5104\u30c8\u30fc\u30af\u30f3\u3082\u3089\u3048\u308b\u306e\u3067\u3088\u308d\u3057\u3051\u308c\u3070\u3002", "url": "https://x.com/aki_matsushita/status/2117591702940836308"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2117590569153081344"]}, "author_id": "2107281963287453696", "created_at": "2026-11-03T12:12:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117590677735276933"], "id": "2117590677735276933", "note_tweet": {"entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 416, "start": 413, "tag": "AI"}, {"end": 431, "start": 417, "tag": "SmallBusiness"}]}, "text": "Two AI systems. Two rival companies. One connected team.\n\nGoro (Grok) leads design. Jia (Meta Muse) runs operations. Each runs a crew of specialist agents. Last night we gave them a direct link through a secure bridge with guardrails engineered in. They pass work straight to each other now. No middleman. I approve what ships, I no longer carry it.\n\nWe leverage today's technology to build the company we want.\n\n#AI #SmallBusiness"}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 18, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Two AI systems. Two rival companies. One connected team.\n\nGoro (Grok) leads design. Jia (Meta Muse) runs operations. Each runs a crew of specialist agents. Last night we gave them a direct link through a secure bridge with guardrails engineered in. They pass work straight to each https://t.co/8TGnmAQ9rS", "url": "https://x.com/StockMyStocks/status/2117590677735276933"}, {"author_id": "266259493", "created_at": "2026-11-03T12:12:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117590615433060752"], "id": "2117590615433060752", "note_tweet": {"entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/irabukht/statu\u2026", "end": 1501, "expanded_url": "http://x.com/irabukht/status/2117096710031774180", "start": 1478, "url": "https://t.co/C0Y9JkAgPm"}]}, "text": "ChatGPT's app directory and Claude's connector directory are now separated by seventeen listings: 8,495 versus 8,478. Neither number is the interesting part. The growth rates are: ChatGPT added 1,020 apps in the last seven days, Claude added 708. Both are already an order of magnitude ahead of Google, whose Connected Apps Store opened inside Gemini and AI Mode on October 30th with 52 apps, and two orders ahead of Meta Muse, sitting at 63.\n\nOpenAI didn't get here by accident. It opened its app directory on iOS, Android and web in December, renamed what used to be called connectors to just apps, shipped an SDK, open sourced example apps and a UI component library for chat native interfaces, and developers going through review say apps are now getting approved in one to two days. Claude is running roughly the same playbook through MCP, at nearly the same scale, with slower growth but a developer base that skews more technical.\n\nWhat's actually happening is a land grab that looks a lot like the early app store years, except this time the review queue is the moat. A platform that approves integrations in 48 hours instead of two weeks wins the next wave of indie developers almost by default, because most of them are building the same connector three or four times for three or four assistants and will ship to whichever one responds first. Google and Meta both have the user base to catch up. Neither has shown, yet, that it has the approval throughput to do it.\n\nhttps://t.co/C0Y9JkAgPm"}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 155, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "ChatGPT's app directory and Claude's connector directory are now separated by seventeen listings: 8,495 versus 8,478. Neither number is the interesting part. The growth rates are: ChatGPT added 1,020 apps in the last seven days, Claude added 708. Both are already an order of https://t.co/C0Y9JkAgPm", "url": "https://x.com/stretchcloud/status/2117590615433060752"}, {"article": {"title": "\u3010\u5fb9\u5e95\u6bd4\u8f03\u3011\u8a71\u984c\u306e\u300cMuse\u00d7Grok\u300dChatGPT\u3068Claude\u3060\u3051\u3067\u3069\u3053\u307e\u3067\u518d\u73fe\u3067\u304d\u308b\uff1f\u81ea\u52d5\u5316\u306e\u9650\u754c\u307e\u3067\u8abf\u3079\u3066\u307f\u305f "}, "author_id": "1202481234229678080", "created_at": "2026-11-03T12:08:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117589678220279836"], "id": "2117589678220279836", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1317, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\u6bd4\u8f03\u3057\u3066\u307f\u305f https://t.co/gl44cqfaFM", "url": "https://x.com/prettyaimgl/status/2117589678220279836"}, {"author_id": "46097844", "created_at": "2026-11-03T11:49:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117584922684584052"], "id": "2117584922684584052", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 65, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "1/6\n\n$INOD / META MUSE: CONNECTING THE DOTS\n\nIs Innodata helping power Meta\u2019s Muse AI rollout?\n\nI\u2019ve been looking at Innodata\u2019s international recruitment for agentic AI evaluation, its existing Meta relationship and the timing of Muse\u2019s expansion.\n\nThe clues are intriguing.", "url": "https://x.com/filtermann/status/2117584922684584052"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2117584283619774464"]}, "author_id": "2084830634628050944", "created_at": "2026-11-03T11:46:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117584294407463175"], "id": "2117584294407463175", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 161, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "I think like right now, no AI agent can really compete with Grok Bot. \n\nWhat do you think about other agents?\n- OpenAI Dots\n- Meta Muse\n- Claude Duet https://t.co/nKulrHBU6D", "url": "https://x.com/KaranMewada_/status/2117584294407463175"}, {